# The ratchet's own prose heuristics.
#
# The five subjects in config.json are checks of the checker: each reproduces a
# defect this repository actually shipped, and each needs arbitrary computation
# (scratch corpora, merge simulation), so they stay scripts. A sixth, the PNG
# round-trip, is at the bottom of this file: it needed the same computation but
# had no defect to reproduce, and so needed rules that could state a refusal.
#
# This one is the other half of the argument -- a standing invariant that needs
# no plumbing at all, and so is written as data instead of as code. If the prose
# form cannot express the invariants of the tool that ships it, it cannot be
# claimed to express anyone else's.

heuristic test-suite
  run      node --test ratchet/dist/test/
  timeout  600000
  applies  when ratchet/dist/test exists
  measure  status  exit code
  measure  failing  number after "# fail"
  measure  passing  number after "# pass"
  rule     failing is 0
  rule     passing is at least 217
  rule     status is one of 0, 1
  rejects  failing 1
  rejects  passing 216
  rejects  status 7
  note     the exit code is measured so that a red suite is judged by its own
  note     counts -- "failing measured 1" -- instead of short-circuiting as a
  note     broken instrument, which is what a nonzero exit means otherwise
  because  a suite that shrinks silently is how a ratchet stops ratcheting: the
  because  count is a floor, raised deliberately, never lowered by accident

# The three below cover the class of defect the corpus was missing.
#
# Classifying the twenty-one v0 review defects against the scripted
# subjects showed every one of those subjects was a check of a data structure:
# five of twenty-one defects, all in one row of the table. The other sixteen
# sat at the process boundary, on the CLI surface, in the capture-path routing
# or in packaging, and none of them had a subject -- because a scratch corpus
# and a deepStrictEqual cannot reach them. The corpus was built where it was
# easy rather than where the bugs live.
#
# Each of these runs a frozen instrument out of {home}, so `replay` and
# `adopt` measure every commit with today's driver instead of whatever that
# commit happened to contain.

heuristic cli-end-to-end
  run      node {home}/tools/e2e.js
  timeout  900000
  owns     .ratchet/tools/e2e.js
  applies  when ratchet/dist/src/index.js exists
  measure  failures  count of lines matching "FAIL "
  measure  declared  number after "scenarios declared:"
  measure  ran  number after "scenarios run:"
  rule     failures is 0
  rule     declared is at least 13
  rule     ran is at least 1
  rejects  failures 1
  rejects  declared 12
  note     each scenario names the guarantee it drives, so a red line is a
  note     sentence about the tool rather than a line number in the driver
  because  the loop in the README -- init, fmt, adopt, verify, break it,
  because  quarantine, reaffirm -- is the product, and running it by hand once
  because  per release is a ritual, not a mechanism

heuristic cli-errors-are-messages
  run      node {home}/tools/error-paths.js
  timeout  600000
  owns     .ratchet/tools/error-paths.js
  applies  when ratchet/dist/src/index.js exists
  measure  traces  count of lines matching "STACK "
  measure  silent  count of lines matching "SILENT "
  measure  homes  number after "broken homes:"
  measure  probed  number after "commands probed:"
  rule     traces is 0
  rule     silent is 0
  rule     homes is 3
  rule     probed is at least 8
  rejects  traces 1
  rejects  silent 1
  because  a stack trace means the failure reached the top of the program
  because  unhandled, so nothing decided what it meant, and the reader learns
  because  the line number of a JSON.parse instead of which file to fix

heuristic source-uniformity
  run      node {home}/tools/uniformity.js
  owns     .ratchet/tools/uniformity.js
  applies  when ratchet/src exists
  measure  violations  count of lines matching "VIOLATION "
  measure  declared  number after "invariants declared:"
  rule     violations is 0
  rule     declared is at least 6
  rejects  violations 1
  rejects  declared 5
  because  partial application of a mechanism -- defined once, wired into some
  because  of its call sites -- has shipped four times in three versions, and a
  because  corpus row cannot catch it: a row is one counterexample and this is
  because  a completeness property over a set of call sites

# This one was a scripted subject and was doing nothing at all.
#
# It could not be armed -- ratchet/src/visual.ts has exactly one commit in this
# repository and was correct in it, so `adopt` had no failure to arm a row
# with -- and a scripted subject with no row is never run by anything. It sat
# in config.json looking like coverage while the visual diff went ungated, and
# the only sign was the validation warning, which reads as paperwork.
#
# The instrument did not need to change: selfcheck.js still does the PNG
# round-trip, still runs out of {home}, and is still owned here so that editing
# it re-opens the proof. Only the judgment moved out of the script and into
# rules that can state what they refuse -- which is the whole point of the
# prose form, and the same shape `test-suite` above already has.

heuristic visual-diff-is-sound
  run      node {home}/tools/selfcheck.js visual-diff-is-sound
  owns     .ratchet/tools/selfcheck.js
  applies  when ratchet/dist/src/visual.js exists
  measure  status  exit code
  measure  verified  count of lines matching "verified on"
  rule     status is 0
  rule     verified is 1
  rejects  status 1
  rejects  verified 0
  note     `verified 0` is the reading that matters: a check can exit 0 without
  note     having asserted anything, and then the green means only that the
  note     process ran. The line is printed last, after every assertion.
  because  a baseline pin is worth exactly what the comparator is worth -- a
  because  diff with a false negative pins nothing, and reports success while
  because  it does it

# The secondary verifier, run inside the gate it attacks.
#
# `ratchet fuzz` mutates synthetic corpus/journal/config/rules state, fuzzes the
# CLI surface, and fuzzes the rules grammar against the oracle invariants (no
# unhandled crash, fsck detects every content-addressed id mismatch, --json is
# honored, fmt is a fixpoint). It has already found three real defects: two
# commands that ignored --json with exit 0, and a formatter that grew a blank
# line into an empty rules file on every run.
#
# The instrument is a wrapper rather than the binary itself, for the same
# reason cli-end-to-end is: the frozen-instrument detector must see a program
# outside the tree it measures, or the gate warns on every commit.

heuristic fuzz-clean
  run      node {home}/tools/fuzz-gate.js
  timeout  600000
  owns     .ratchet/tools/fuzz-gate.js
  applies  when ratchet/dist/src/index.js exists
  measure  status  exit code
  rule     status is 0
  rejects  status 1
  because  the fuzzer must stay clean against a fixed seed, or a regression in
  because  the gate's own machinery is discovered only after it ships
